### Set up OTLP HTTP trace exporter in Node.js

Source: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/blob/main/experimental/packages/exporter-trace-otlp-http/README.md

Configure and initialize the OTLP trace exporter for HTTP transport in Node.js. The exporter sends spans as JSON over HTTP to the specified collector URL, with optional custom headers and concurrency limit. The BatchSpanProcessor batches spans with a maximum queue size and export interval.

```js
const { trace } = require('@opentelemetry/api');
const { TracerProvider, BatchSpanProcessor } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace');
const { OTLPTraceExporter } =  require('@opentelemetry/exporter-trace-otlp-http');

const collectorOptions = {
  url: '<opentelemetry-collector-url>', // url is optional and can be omitted - default is http://localhost:4318/v1/traces
  headers: {
    foo: 'bar'
  }, // an optional object containing custom headers to be sent with each request will only work with http
  concurrencyLimit: 10, // an optional limit on pending requests
};

const exporter = new OTLPTraceExporter(collectorOptions);
const tracerProvider = new TracerProvider({
  spanProcessors: [
    new BatchSpanProcessor({
      exporter,
      // The maximum queue size. After the size is reached spans are dropped.
      maxQueueSize: 1000,
      // The interval between two consecutive exports
      scheduledDelayMillis: 30000,
    })
  ]
});
trace.setGlobalTracerProvider(tracerProvider);
```

